 "item", "numeric-id": 1032, "id": "Q1032"}, "type": "wikibase-entityid"}, "datatype": "wikibase-item"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9657$393F2183-6E25-4C28-B26E-B242E0EB1AAD", "rank": "normal"}], "P19": [{"mainsnak": {"snaktype": "value", "property": "P19", "hash": "ae50da52804db47e528a27fa511988112f9be900", "datavalue": {"value": "Yeah. There was a club on 47th Street. I think at the Club 409. The people like Muddy Water, Sunnyland Slim, used to work there. I'd go by there and hear everybody. In fact I worked with Sunnyland and Memphis Slim, Roosevelt Sykes. Because in Chicago a lot of times if musicians wanted to work regular you had to work with Blues groups, you know what I mean. So I got the opportunity, which was ve...", "type": "string"}, "datatype": "string"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9657$9E214F4C-87EA-4ED5-920B-7631DEC3FDB3", "rank": "normal"}]}}